    "question": "Which note-taking method is most effective for actually retaining and using what you learn?",
    "summary": "Not all note-taking methods support long-term retention equally. Methods that incorporate active recall, elaborative encoding, and spaced review—such as the Cornell Method, Zettelkasten, and the Feynman Technique—consistently outperform passive transcription for retaining and applying what you learn.",
